Key codes use the platform's native keyboard code space. Register listeners before Start(), and call Stop() when observation is no longer needed.

```cpp
KeyboardMonitor monitor;
monitor.AddListener<KeyPressedEvent>([](const KeyPressedEvent& event) {
  const auto native_key = event.GetKeycode();
  (void)native_key;
});
monitor.Start();
```
